logo-discord.svg, logo-slack.svg, logo-mattermost.svg, logo-telegram.svg
and logo-pushover.svg (the notification channels), and logo-git.svg,
logo-github.svg, logo-gitlab.svg, logo-docker.svg, logo-postgres.svg,
logo-mysql.svg, logo-mariadb.svg, logo-mongodb.svg, logo-redis.svg,
logo-clickhouse.svg, logo-cloudflared.svg, logo-minio.svg, logo-n8n.svg,
logo-uptime-kuma.svg and logo-wordpress.svg (what the Add resource page
offers) are from the selfh.st icon collection
(https://selfh.st/icons, https://github.com/selfhst/icons), which is
licensed under Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International
(https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/).

Changed here: each style attribute is written as the presentation
attributes it stands for (style="fill:#5865f2" is fill="#5865f2"), since
the dashboard's content security policy drops a style attribute, and a
<style> element of classes is written onto what had the class, for the
same reason. Nothing else of a file is changed.

The collection has no SVG of three:

logo-ghost.svg is the outline from Simple Icons
(https://simpleicons.org, CC0 1.0), in Ghost's own black on a white disc.

logo-keydb.svg and logo-dragonfly.svg are the outlines from Coolify's
public/svgs (https://github.com/coollabsio/coolify, Apache License 2.0),
which draws them in one colour. Changed here: the colours are those of
each owner's own icon (KeyDB's favicon; the two ends of the gradient in
Dragonfly's logo), and the editor's metadata is removed.

Each logo is a trademark of its owner and is used only to name that
owner's service.

logo-email.svg and logo-webhook.svg are musdash's own. The outline of the
webhook mark is Hugeicons' (MIT licence, ../ui/icons.LICENSE).
